    "type": "archive Q&A",
    "topic": "openlifescienceai/medmcqa",
    "problem": "Q: Here is a problem to solve. Which of the following will cause an increase in the prevalence of disease? A) Immigration of healthy persons B) Increased cure rate of disease C) Longer duration of disease D) Increased death rate in disease",
    "solution": "A: Answer: C) Longer duration of disease Explanation: Prevalence depends upon 2 factors, the incidence (I) and duration of illness (D). Given the assumption that the population is stable, and incidence and duration are unchanging, the relationship between incidence and prevalence is, P = I* D = Incidence * mean duration Thus when duration increases prevalence also increases. Ref: Park's Textbook\u2026",
    "source": "huggingface"
  }
